when you think of crypto traders what do  you think do you imagine young guys and  hoodies living in their parents  basements  yeah maybe in 2012  but today that stereotype is a bit  outdated crypto has gone corporate in a  big way  just last year professional money  managers bought and sold more than a  trillion dollars worth of crypto so  let's talk about the new cryptocurrency  market i'm going to give you the three  reasons that wall street has taken over  crypto  let's get into it  reason number one  fomo or fear of missing out when there's  money to be made folks on wall street  want to get their hands on it and crypto  is generating a lot of money the market  cap or total value of all cryptocurrency  investments is approaching two trillion  dollars that's tiny compared to the 40  trillion dollars or so of market cap on  the s p 500 but 2 trillion dollars is  still a lot of money and with crypto's  continued growth in the mainstream  acceptance there are lots of  opportunities for more management fees  trading commissions and other revenue  streams that wall street loves many also  see crypto as the first new asset class  in a generation that creates all sorts  of new opportunities for new clients and  more gains  reason number two the crypto market has  grown up  it used to be that to invest in  cryptocurrency you had to buy the coins  yourself or mine them and then find a  secure way to hold them today there are  crypto derivatives like futures options  and swaps plus plenty of exchanges and  market makers that make investing in  cryptocurrency a lot more palatable for  the risk-averse wall street crowd the  market has also grown significantly in a  short amount of time rising from a  market cap of around 150 billion dollars  in march 2020 to 1.7 trillion dollars in  march 2022  that growth means that professional  money managers can safely make big bets  without moving the entire market or  drawing undue attention these new  products and deeper markets also make it  possible for firms to make money on  crypto through price volatility so they  win whether prices go up or down that  wasn't possible when all you could do  was buy or sell tokens reason number  three  there are a growing number of crypto  converts on wall street just like more  everyday people are starting to believe  in crypto more professional investors  are as well my colleague gregory  zuckerman reported earlier this year  that billionaire hedge fund manager paul  tudor jones's firm is investing in  crypto as a way to protect against  inflation european hedge fund brevan  howard has even created a cryptocurrency  division which manages over 250 million  dollars the 1.14 trillion dollars in  trading the professional investors did  in 2021 for crypto exchange coinbase was  almost 10 times the amount of trading  they did in 2020 and it's more than  double the 535 billion dollars in  trading done by retail investors  according to my colleague paul vina that  shows just how big a slice of the crypto  pie wall street is taking none of that  means that crypto is guaranteed to make  you rich or that it's a totally safe  investment now just because wall street  is doing it doesn't mean it's a good  idea just know that more trades in the  crypto market are being made by folks  who look like this  than folks who look like this if you  enjoyed this video be sure to like and  subscribe and i encourage you to be like  the great warren g who said shake the  spot with my knot  may fade because i don't like to dream  about getting paid  i'll see you next time
 

